From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:59:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] clutter: take the grain of blurs from a blue-noise tile

The grain blurs add to hide banding came from a hash that leaves clumps
and lines when looked at closely. It now comes from a 64 pixel tile of
blue noise, sampled once per pixel, which spreads it evenly at every
scale. Effects that draw blurs with a shader of their own can sample the
same tile, so all glass has the same grain.

Upstream-Status: luft-only Kestrel's glass grain
